<title>MONGOLIA: MONGOLIA JAN-JULY COPPER OUTPUT UP YR/YR 20 PCT.</title>
<headline>MONGOLIA JAN-JULY COPPER OUTPUT UP YR/YR 20 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>ULAN BATOR 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mongolia's output of copper concentrate rose 20 percent to 249,800 tonnes in the first seven months of 1997, up from 208,100 tonnes in the year-ago period, the State Statistics Bulletin said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Exports of copper concentrate between January and July fell 16.05 percent to 247,900 tonnes compared with 295,300 tonnes in the same 1996 period, the bulletin said.</p>
<p>It gave no further details.</p>
<p>-- Ulan Bator Newsroom (976) 1-312 565</p>
</text>
